Actually, most of the stuff is MS-DOS Turbo-Pascal and not Windows (the 
random sentence generator is in ancient Basic).  Cowan's parser is in 
portable C, I believe, but Nora wrote the other stuff never expecting it to 
be used other than on an MS-DOS machine.  LogFlash source is now up there, 
and her other Turbo programs use about half of the LogFlash code as common 
routines for screen management, so you would be advised to look and see 
what you make of that code before tackling anything else.  So far, no one 
has successfully ported LogFlash to any other system, though many have 
tried; Turbo_Pascal is apparently quite unlike curses (that is the only 
screen package that I KNOW has been tried).

